# TEMPLATE ONLY - this file is committed to git, so never put real keys here.
#
# Put your credentials in env.txt (or .env) instead; both are gitignored.
# On Windows, env.txt is the easy one: Explorer cannot create dot-files.
#
# Only the anon/publishable key belongs here. It is public by design and ships
# to the browser; Row Level Security is what protects the data. NEVER put the
# service-role key in this file or anywhere else in the frontend — it bypasses
# RLS entirely.
#
# Leaving these unset is supported: the app then runs local-first exactly as it
# did before, which is how the artifact and read-only share builds work.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
